      {
        "category": "summary",
        "text": "Security update for screen",
        "title": "Title of the patch"
      },
      {
        "category": "description",
        "text": "This update for screen fixes the following issues:\n\nSecurity issues fixed:\n    \n- CVE-2025-46802: temporary `chmod` of a user's TTY to mode 0666 when attempting to attach to a multi-user session\n  allows for TTY hijacking (bsc#1242269).\n\nOther issues fixed:\n\n- Use TTY file descriptor passing after a suspend (`MSG_CONT`).\n",
        "title": "Description of the patch"
      },
